From 39012c21c4d8abbf656122e89b7c34549f37c3d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:23:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Gateway inflow/outflow per 30 km stretch of the line, not per
 face

On a staircase each face measures the flow normal to itself, so flow along the line goes in
through one face and out through the next: per-face inflow and outflow were inflated (Fram
20.6/24.2 Sv in the model against 10.7/13.2 in GLORYS, with the same net). Transports are now
added up over 30 km stretches and level, the same bins for model and GLORYS, before the split;
the mean sections use the same bins.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AbhhvncDb1PnxFVHRBrPRS
